{
  "id": "23198_agaku",
  "headword": "{足掻|あが}く",
  "reading": "あがく",
  "romaji": "agaku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to struggle; to flounder",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to struggle; to flounder; to thrash about",
      "explanation": "To make desperate, often futile efforts to escape a difficult situation or to resist an inevitable outcome."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "23198_agaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{足掻|あが}いても{無駄|むだ}だ。",
      "english": "It's useless to struggle.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23198_agaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{最後|さいご}まで{足掻|あが}き{続|つづ}けた。",
      "english": "I kept struggling until the very end.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "23198_agaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{借金|しゃっきん}に{追|お}われて{足掻|あが}いているが、なかなか{抜|ぬ}け{出|だ}せない。",
      "english": "I'm struggling under debt, but I can't seem to get out of it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Originally described a horse stamping or pawing the ground restlessly. The modern meaning emphasizes desperate, often futile resistance against a difficult situation. Often carries a negative nuance suggesting the effort may be in vain.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {足掻|あが}いても{無駄|むだ}: struggling is futile\n- {必死|ひっし}に{足掻|あが}く: to struggle desperately\n- じたばた{足掻|あが}く: to thrash about helplessly\n- {悪足掻|わるあが}き: vain struggle, futile resistance\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- もがく: to writhe, to struggle — more physical, often used for struggling in water or against physical restraint\n- {悪足掻|わるあが}きする: to put up a futile struggle — specifically implies the effort is pointless",
